### Example 1 Full Visual Verification (Workbook p. 33)
Use the graph to identify the following:
- **$x$-intercept:** \underline{\hspace{2cm}}
- **$y$-intercept:** \underline{\hspace{2cm}}
- **Slope ($m$):** \underline{\hspace{2cm}}

solution:
$$\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{x\text{-intercept: }} & \mathbf{(3, 0)} \quad (\text{where line crosses horizontal axis}) \\
\mathbf{y\text{-intercept: }} & \mathbf{(0, 2)} \quad (\text{where line crosses vertical axis}) \\
\mathbf{\text{Slope } m: } & \mathbf{-\frac{2}{3}} = \frac{\text{Rise}}{\text{Run}} = \frac{-2}{+3}
\end{aligned}$$

$$\begin{aligned}
\text{Compare with } y = mx + b: \\[0.5em]
\mathbf{\text{Slope } m: } & \mathbf{\frac{1}{4}} \quad (\text{Up 1, Right 4}) \\[0.5em]
\mathbf{y\text{-intercept: }} & \mathbf{(0, -6)}
\end{aligned}$$
